    "result_text": "All tests green (3/3). Here's what I did.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded an optional 4-digit `postcode` to owners, validated against the city's region only when present, and stored/returned on the owner.\n\n**How the behaviour was kept as small, low-coupling additions:**\n- The postcode round-trips (persist + return) entirely through **auto-mapping** \u2014 because both the generated DTOs and the `Owner` entity now expose `postcode`, MapStruct maps it in both directions and no mapper, `BuildOwner`, `ApplyOwner`, or responder code was touched.\n- Validation is one new **cohesive function** with zero surrounding complexity (single method, no siblings): `EnsureOwnerPostcode` reads `@Val Owner`, short-circuits when the postcode is absent, rejects a non-4-digit value, and \u2014 for a city whose region is known via the existing `Locality` table \u2014 enforces the NSW/VIC/QLD ranges. Unknown region \u21d2 any 4-digit accepted.\n- Errors follow the repo's established pattern: a checked `InvalidPostcodeException` + handler (400) wired via an escalation YAML, rather than growing any existing handler.\n\n**Files changed (9):**\n1. `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the `postcode` property to `OwnerFields` (flows into both request and response DTOs).\n2. `model/Owner.java` \u2014 field + trivial getter/setter.\n3. `function/owner/EnsureOwnerPostcode.java` \u2014 new validation step.\n4. `escalation/InvalidPostcodeException.java` \u2014 new checked exception.\n5. `escalation/InvalidPostcodeExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 new 400 handler.\n6. `officefloor/escalation/...InvalidPostcodeException.yml` \u2014 escalation wiring.\n7. `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted `ensurePostcode` step right after `build`.\n8. `db/hsqldb/schema.sql` \u2014 `postcode` column (test DB; ddl-auto handles h2).\n9. `db/hsqldb/data.sql` \u2014 one `NULL` added to the 10 positional owner seed inserts to match the new column.\n\nTests: `coreStoresValidPostcode`, `coreAcceptsOwnerWithoutPostcode`, `errorRejectsMalformedPostcode` \u2014 all pass, full suite green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\nOne scoping note: I implemented this for the create (POST) path, which is what the spec (\"an owner created with\u2026\") and the new tests exercise. The PUT/update pipeline (`ApplyOwner`) doesn't copy `postcode` today, so I left it untouched to avoid touching more code; say the word if you'd like postcode edits supported on update too.",
